    "section_evoo_v3_faq_rRJhLR": {
      "type": "section-evoo-v3-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_item_BFc6Am": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "I've never heard of yeast protein — is it proven?",
            "answer": "<p>Fermented yeast protein achieves PDCAAS 1.0 — the FAO/WHO maximum protein quality score. This is the same standard that whey, egg white, and casein achieve. It contains all 9 essential amino acids at or above human requirements. It's not a novel concept — yeast has been a food-grade protein source for decades; the fermentation and extraction process is what concentrates and purifies the protein to a quality comparable to animal sources. Every batch is independently tested at a NABL-accredited laboratory. The COA is downloadable via the QR code on the pack.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_pgG9dR": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Will it actually taste good?",
            "answer": "<p>AIWO Yeast Protein is flavoured with Kesar Badam — Saffron and Almond — and sweetened exclusively with Monk Fruit, which has a clean, sweet profile without the bitter aftertaste common in stevia. It is designed to mix into almond milk, smoothies, oats, or yogurt. It does not contain sucralose, aspartame, or acesulfame-K — the artificial sweeteners responsible for the chemical aftertaste in many protein powders.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_zet6LP": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "25g protein sounds high — is it safe?",
            "answer": "<p>25g per serving is within the range identified in research as optimal for stimulating muscle protein synthesis (20–40g per serving, Phillips & Van Loon, J Sports Sci, 2011). It is below the threshold at which protein causes gastrointestinal distress in healthy individuals. The inclusion of a 5-enzyme digestive blend, probiotic, and prebiotic specifically addresses digestive tolerance. Individuals with kidney conditions should consult a physician before high-protein supplementation.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_Q6TUxh": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why not just use whey?",
            "answer": "<p>If you tolerate whey and have no dairy concerns, whey is an excellent protein. But 65%+ of South Asian adults have some degree of lactose intolerance — making whey a poor match for most of the Indian market. AIWO Fermented Yeast Protein achieves the same PDCAAS 1.0 quality as whey, without any dairy derivatives, without lactose, and with a three-layer gut support formula that makes it genuinely appropriate for sensitive stomachs.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_item_WyBt4K": {
          "type": "faq_item",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Why is the price what it is?",
